    state: open
  - id: D:question/json-written-unsure
    type: question
    about: C:reliance/json-written
    asks: 'Is this right, and if not, what is? "JSON is written on one line with ", " between items and ": " after
      keys; every character outside ASCII is written as a backslash, u and four lowercase hex digits (a pair of
      them for a character beyond U+FFFF), and control characters likewise, except the short escapes for quote,
      backslash, line feed, carriage return, tab, backspace and form feed; numbers are written as in the entry on
      numbers written as text; not-a-number and the infinities are written NaN, Infinity and -Infinity."'
    why: unsure
    kind: text
    to: maker
    raised:
      by: move
      from: question
      at: 2026-11-18 12:45:00+00:00
      run: 2026-11-18-1245-a905
    state: open
  - id: D:question/json-keys-sorted-unsure
    type: question
    about: C:reliance/json-keys-sorted
    asks: Is this right, and if not, what is? "Asked to sort keys, JSON is written with each object's keys in code-point
      order."
    why: unsure
    kind: text
    to: maker
    raised:
      by: move
      from: question
      at: 2026-11-18 12:45:00+00:00
      run: 2026-11-18-1245-a905
    state: open
  - id: D:question/json-read-unsure
    type: question
    about: C:reliance/json-read
    asks: Is this right, and if not, what is? "JSON is read with white space (space, tab, line feed, carriage return)
      allowed around values; a number without a fraction or an exponent becomes a whole number of any size, exactly,
      any other a fractional number; NaN, Infinity and -Infinity are accepted; a raw control character inside a
      string is refused; a key given twice keeps its last value; anything else is refused with a decoding error,
      a kind of value error."
    why: unsure
    kind: text
    to: maker
    raised:
      by: move
      from: question
      at: 2026-11-18 12:45:00+00:00
      run: 2026-11-18-1245-a905
    state: open
  - id: D:question/home-and-tilde-unsure
    type: question
    about: C:reliance/home-and-tilde
    asks: Is this right, and if not, what is? "The home folder is the HOME variable when it is set, else the account's
      entry in the system's password database."
    why: unsure
